DESCRIPTION:https://sf.funcheap.com/sfs-free-opera-day-outdoor-concert-13-
 opera-companies-transamerica-redwood-park/\nLocation: san jose\nPrice: Fre
 e\nCategories: concert\, free\nSource: funcheap/san-jose+funcheap/san-fran
 cisco\n\nThirteen Bay Area opera companies present a free outdoor concert 
 at Redwood Park\, located at the base of San Francisco’s Transamerica Py
 ramid Center. The event features curated performances spanning three centu
 ries of opera\, with Bay Area composer Carla Lucero serving as emcee. Atte
 ndees must register in advance via Eventbrite. A bar will be available for
  purchase\, and professional photography will be present. Original Event D
 escription: 13 Bay Area opera companies unite for a free outdoor concert a
 t the Transamerica Pyramid Center Redwood Park. Sunday\, September 20\, 1
 –5 PM. Opera Day in the Bay Sunday\, September 20\, 1–5 p.m. at the Re
 dwood Park at the base of San Francisco’s iconic Transamerica Pyramid Ce
 nter. Enter the park at 545 Sansome Street\, between Washington and Clay S
 treets. Opera Day in the Bay brings together Ars Minerva\, Festival Opera\
 , Lamplighters Music Theatre\, Livermore Valley Opera\, Mercury Opera Thea
 ter\, Opera Parallèle\, Opera San José\, Pocket Opera\, Sacramento Philh
 armonic & Opera\, San Francisco Opera Guild\, Upspark Productions\, West E
 dge Opera — each performing a curated selection that showcases their uni
 que artistic voice. The program spans more than three cen
LOCATION:san jose
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/sfs-free-opera-day-outdoor-concert-13-opera-co
 mpanies-transamerica-redwood-park/
END:VEVENT
